    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.ai\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI am experiencing a bug with the `mini.ai` plugin. When the cursor is inside a pair of quotes and I try to select the text in that pair (`viq`) , the plugin jumps to the next pair of quotes and select its content. This also happens with the other types of pairs (brackets, etc.), and sometimes with the \"around\" version (`vaq`).\r\n\r\nThe search method is correctly set to `cover_or_next`.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.2\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. Open a file (Typescript here) and type `const list = [\"abc\", \"def\"]`\r\n3. Position the cursor on \"a\" and run `viq`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nI expect the string `abc` to be selected.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nThe string `def` is actually selected.",
    "closed_at": "2023-10-09T15:07:56Z",
