            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue.\r\n\r\nI can not reproduce and pretty sure everything works correctly here. Can you still reproduce with minimal config (ideally only with 'mini.ai' enabled)?\r\n\r\nHere are the possible causes of your behavior:\r\n- When it comes to quotes, [they](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0c50ef9d0b7cae1145f3365e7bcf9ed01bc00005/doc/mini-ai.txt#L150-L154) are [balanced](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0c50ef9d0b7cae1145f3365e7bcf9ed01bc00005/doc/mini-ai.txt#L371-L374). So in this example it would select `def` if cursor is on comma.\r\n- When target selection contains single character and cursor is on it, applying `i` textobject would trigger \"consecutive application\" (as target region is already already selected after `v`) and try to select other region.\r\n- When there are both multiline covering region and target region on same line, [the latter will be selected](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0c50ef9d0b7cae1145f3365e7bcf9ed01bc00005/doc/mini-ai.txt#L424-L426).\r\n- Having conflicting set of mappings. What does `xmap i` show? It should not have `iq` (or other combinations with which you have problems).\r\n\r\nClosing as I really doubt that this basic feature does not work because of 'mini.ai'. If you are indeed able to reproduce with only 'mini.ai', please let me know.",
